 (CT-L, T-L, and C-L) reside within the <italic>&#x003b2;</italic>-subunits of 20S and interact with proteasome inhibitors. Bortezomib and NPI-0052 are structurally distinct with different active sites.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="95-6603406f1"/></fig><fig id="fig2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>NPI-0052- and Bortezomib-induced cell-death signalling pathways. Both NPI-0052 and Bortezomib trigger intrinsic (caspase-9-mediated) and extrinsic (caspase-8-mediated) apoptotic signalling pathways. Deletion of Bax&#x0002f;Bak results in significant loss of response to Bortezomib, but not NPI-0052.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="95-6603406f2"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>